NNAAMMEE
       addpart - tell the kernel about the existence of a partition

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       aaddddppaarrtt _d_e_v_i_c_e _p_a_r_t_i_t_i_o_n _s_t_a_r_t _l_e_n_g_t_h

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       aaddddppaarrtt tells the Linux kernel about the existence of the specified
       partition. The command is a simple wrapper around the "add partition"
       ioctl.

       This command doesn’t manipulate partitions on a block device.

PPAARRAAMMEETTEERRSS
       _d_e_v_i_c_e
           The disk device.

       _p_a_r_t_i_t_i_o_n
           The partition number.

       _s_t_a_r_t
           The beginning of the partition (in 512-byte sectors).

       _l_e_n_g_t_h
           The length of the partition (in 512-byte sectors).

       --hh, ----hheellpp
           Display help text and exit.

       --VV, ----vveerrssiioonn
           Print version and exit.

